& [AuthorizedFileSet] is exact
  + [workspace] is Cargo.toml and Cargo.lock
  + [crate_manifest] is crates/cantor_windows_preflight/Cargo.toml
  + [production] is crates/cantor_windows_preflight/src/lib.rs
  + [physical_probe] is crates/cantor_windows_preflight/examples/physical_probe.rs
  + [contract_tests] is crates/cantor_windows_preflight/tests/runtime_contract.rs
  + [physical_runner] is scripts/run_windows_platform_preflight_fixture.ps1
  + [evidence_builder] is scripts/build_windows_platform_preflight_runtime_evidence_manifest.ps1
  + [evidence_test] is crates/cantor_windows_preflight/tests/runtime_evidence.rs
  + [evidence_manifest] is crates/cantor_windows_preflight/evidence/windows_platform_preflight_runtime_evidence_manifest.json
  + [physical_evidence] is crates/cantor_windows_preflight/evidence/windows_platform_preflight_physical_observation.json
  + [governance] is source, canonical, exploded, justification, plan, matrix, slice, registry, solution, proof, review, fault, file-change, turn, map, narrative, readiness, reentry, and conversation records
  - never: change an existing production Rust source file

& [DependencyContract] is exact
  + [new_workspace_member] is crates/cantor_windows_preflight
  + [project_dependency] is cantor_ecosystem by local path
  + [wire_dependencies] are workspace serde and serde_json
  + [Windows_dependency] is windows-sys exactly 0.61.2 with default features false
  + [Windows_features] are Win32_Foundation, Win32_Security, and Win32_Storage_FileSystem
  + [registry_package_delta] is zero
  + [lock_delta] is one new local package entry and its existing dependency edges only
  + [existing_package_versions_sources_checksums] remain unchanged

& [CrateSafetyContract] is isolated
  + [crate_default] is deny unsafe_code and deny unsafe_op_in_unsafe_fn
  + [Windows_module] is private and cfg(windows)
  + [module_exception] is allow unsafe_code
  + [unsafe_blocks] is exactly six
  + [unsafe_functions] is zero
  + [each_block] has one immediately preceding SAFETY comment stating pointer, size, initialization, lifetime, error, or ownership invariants
  + [existing_crates] retain workspace unsafe_code forbid

& [PublicRuntimeContract] is safe
  + [constant] is WINDOWS_PLATFORM_PREFLIGHT_RUNTIME_PROFILE
  + [function] is observe_platform_preflight
  + [input] is borrowed WindowsPlatformPreflightRequest
  + [output] is Result<WindowsPlatformPreflightRecord, WindowsPlatformPreflightRuntimeFault>
  + [runtime_fault] is InvalidRequest with bounded proven form fault, UnsupportedTarget, or OperatingSystemErrorUnavailable
  + [runtime_operation] is Open or Query with the exact PlatformPreflightQueryStage
  + [request_validation] precedes cfg target dispatch and every possible Windows call
  + [released_record] passes ValidatePlatformPreflightForm

& [NonWindowsContract] is explicit
  + [windows_sys_import] is absent
  + [FFI] is absent
  + [result] is UnsupportedTarget after request validation
  + [physical_claim] is absent

& [OpenContract] is exact
  + [function] is CreateFileW
  + [path] is one owned NUL-terminated UTF-16 copy of validated input_root
  + [desired_access] is FILE_READ_ATTRIBUTES
  + [share_mode] is FILE_SHARE_READ plus FILE_SHARE_WRITE plus FILE_SHARE_DELETE
  + [creation_disposition] is OPEN_EXISTING
  + [flags] are FILE_FLAG_OPEN_REPARSE_POINT plus FILE_FLAG_BACKUP_SEMANTICS
  + [security_attributes] is null
  + [template_handle] is null
  + [failure] is INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE followed immediately by GetLastError
  + [zero_error] becomes OperatingSystemErrorUnavailable for Open and never an OS fault or invented query stage
  + [success] transfers exactly once into OwnedHandle

& [OwnershipContract] is one-way
  + [precondition] rejects INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE before FromRawHandle
  + [transfer] is one OwnedHandle::from_raw_handle
  + [borrow] uses AsRawHandle for calls while the owner is live
  + [escape] is none
  + [direct_CloseHandle] is forbidden
  + [drop] is the only closure mechanism
  + [released_result] contains no resource identity other than copied strong file identity

& [QueryContract] is exact order on one handle
  + [Q1] is GetFileInformationByHandleEx FileIdInfo into MaybeUninit<FILE_ID_INFO>
  + [Q2] is GetFinalPathNameByHandleW FILE_NAME_NORMALIZED plus VOLUME_NAME_GUID into [u16; 32768]
  + [Q3] is GetVolumeInformationByHandleW into [u16; 261] label, three u32 scalars, and [u16; 261] filesystem name
  + [Q4] is GetFileInformationByHandleEx FileRemoteProtocolInfo into MaybeUninit<FILE_REMOTE_PROTOCOL_INFO>
  + [fixed_structure_size] uses checked u32 conversion of size_of
  + [success_only] permits assume_init or output consumption
  + [failure] captures GetLastError in the same unsafe block before another FFI call
  + [zero_error] becomes OperatingSystemErrorUnavailable for the exact query stage

& [OutputTransformationContract] is strict
  + [identity] is u64 VolumeSerialNumber and 16 FileId.Identifier bytes encoded as 32 lowercase hexadecimal digits in array order
  + [final_path] consumes exactly the successful returned character count
  + [final_path_return_zero] is QueryFault FinalVolumeGuidPath with actual nonzero error
  + [final_path_return_at_or_above_capacity] is ObservationFault ReturnedLengthLimit
  + [text] uses String::from_utf16 without replacement
  + [volume_text] requires an in-buffer NUL terminator
  + [remote_reserved] requires Reserved, GenericReserved.Reserved, and ProtocolSpecific.Reserved all zero
  + [invalid_UTF16] is ObservationFault InvalidUtf16 at the producing stage
  + [invalid_length_or_terminator] is ObservationFault ReturnedLengthLimit or InvalidObservation
  + [invalid_structure_or_form] is ObservationFault InvalidObservation
  + [zero_after_reported_failure] is a runtime provenance fault with no error code, partial evidence, or result claim
  + [partial_evidence] is absent

& [DispositionContract] is inherited
  + [remote_protocol_nonzero] is RejectRemoteProtocol
  + [protocol_zero_and_filesystem_NTFS] is EligibleLocalNtfs
  + [protocol_zero_and_other_filesystem] is RejectUnsupportedFileSystem
  + [final_validation] is authoritative

& [ExactCallSet] is closed
  + [allowed] is CreateFileW
  + [allowed] is GetLastError
  + [allowed] is GetFileInformationByHandleEx with FileIdInfo
  + [allowed] is GetFinalPathNameByHandleW
  + [allowed] is GetVolumeInformationByHandleW
  + [allowed] is GetFileInformationByHandleEx with FileRemoteProtocolInfo
  - never: call CloseHandle, ReadFile, write, delete, rename, enumerate, stream, privilege, device-control, process, network, clock, or random APIs

& [DefaultVerificationContract] is effect free
  + [physical_probe] is ignored
  + [unit_tests] cover invalid request, non-Windows dispatch where applicable, strict text conversion, identity encoding, reserved values, disposition, local fault classification, and final form validation
  + [static_test] asserts six unsafe blocks, six SAFETY comments, exact call set and flags, private module exception, and forbidden API and access absence
  + [debug_and_release] run without physical opt-in

& [PhysicalFixtureContract] is separately explicit
  + [host] is the current x86_64-pc-windows-msvc desktop
  + [fixture_root] is \\?\C:\Project\Cantor\.local\m2b-platform-preflight-fixture
  + [runner_repository_root] is C:\Project\Cantor
  + [allowed_mutation] is create that directory and write request and transient result files below it
  + [forbidden_mutation] is every path outside that fixture root
  + [probe] is opt-in and executes only after exact root and repository assertions
  + [observation] performs only the authorized read-only call set
  + [expected_result] is Complete with protocol zero, filesystem NTFS, EligibleLocalNtfs, valid strong identity, and canonical volume-GUID final path
  + [unexpected_result] is preserved and blocks physical-success closure
  + [cleanup] is not performed

& [PhysicalEvidenceContract] is bound
  + [record] contains runtime profile, captured-at time, exact request, exact result, host OS, rustc host, filesystem precondition, source commit, executable SHA-256, Cargo.lock SHA-256, and fixture-root identity
  + [authority] is this signature UUID
  + [claim] is limited to the recorded run
  + [candidate_or_scanner_inference] is forbidden

& [RequirementSet] is M2B-WPR-001 through M2B-WPR-018
  + [lineage] preserves source and prior proofs
  + [runtime] fixes crate, API, target dispatch, dependencies, and forms
  + [resource] fixes open, owner, calls, buffers, and errors
  + [provenance] fixes OS, local, complete, and no-partial outcomes
  + [physical] fixes the exact opt-in fixture and evidence
  + [closure] fixes focused, global, static, audit, evidence, rollback, support, and publication proof

& [Acceptance] is exact
  + [static] exact files, dependencies, call set, flags, six unsafe blocks, comments, and forbidden surface pass
  + [focused] runtime pure and no-call paths pass in debug and overflow-checked release
  + [physical] the governed exact-root probe emits and validates the expected Complete result
  + [global] workspace debug, release, format, warnings-denied lint, release build, warnings-denied docs, and audit pass
  + [evidence] current manifests verify after narrative closure
  + [review] readiness advances only the directly observed gates

& [AuthorityBoundary] is one runtime and fixture only
  + [allowed] is the exact new crate, safe API, six-block Windows seam, exact ignored probe, exact local fixture mutation, read-only root observation, evidence, and proof
  + [forbidden] is existing production Rust change, seventh unsafe block, new Win32 call, write access, traversal, content, stream, attributes, case policy, scanner, receipt, candidate, sandbox, cleanup, launch, seal, promotion, or non-fixture mutation

& [SJSProcessingTrace] is complete
  + [source_preserved] is raw source plus immutable manifest and prior bindings
  + [delineated] is request, runtime dispatch, resource seam, result, physical probe, and scanner absence
  + [exploded] is eighteen requirements, sixteen constraints, eighteen failures, and ten verification gates
  + [semantically_refined] is runtime, unsafe, read-only, physical success, and complete meaning
  + [constraint_checked] is official Microsoft semantics, Rust ownership, generated bindings, and prior proofs
  + [pruned] is traversal, content, streams, retries, broad unsafe, automatic physical execution, scanner, and receipt
  + [data_design_checked] is validated request, runtime fault sum, proven result sum, one owner, and bound physical bundle
  + [exhaustion_reviewed] is seven_fold_phase_locked
  + [justified] is claim, support, false options, counterarguments, invalidation, and rollback
  + [planned] is ordered authority, implementation, physical proof, global verification, evidence, and publication work
  + [registry_recorded] is graph-addressable nodes, causal edges, retrieval terms, and nonedges

